1726 0 obj
<</Title(At the time, the main focus was on ergonomics, but that led to a huge oversight: we didn't add enough thickness \(1 mm\) to the cover after adding fillets and some surface curves, which caused the 3D print to feel like single-line threads on some portions and even break when a force was applied to it. Similarly, the casing didn't have enough tolerance for the cover.)/Dest[24 0 R/Fit]/Parent 1629 0 R/Next 1727 0 R>>
endobj

1727 0 obj
<</Title(The fix was to redo the model in SolidWorks and allocate a thickness of 2.5 mm and a tolerance of 0.5mm)/Dest[24 0 R/Fit]/Parent 1629 0 R/Prev 1726 0 R>>
endobj

